00:09:30.640 --> 00:09:34.760
food, so I try to keep eating out to a

00:09:32.560 --> 00:09:36.880
minimum. Every time you feed yourself

00:09:34.760 --> 00:09:38.600
something real and wholesome, you're

00:09:36.880 --> 00:09:40.120
keeping the most basic promise to

00:09:38.600 --> 00:09:41.880
yourself, which is to keep yourself

00:09:40.120 --> 00:09:43.920
healthy and nourished. And it doesn't

00:09:41.880 --> 00:09:46.240
even have to be expensive to be healthy.

00:09:43.920 --> 00:09:48.160
Number seven is learning financial

00:09:46.240 --> 00:09:49.800
literacy. Quick disclaimer, I'm not a

00:09:48.160 --> 00:09:52.040
financial advisor, but things like your

00:09:49.800 --> 00:09:53.760
credit score can affect a lot of things.

00:09:52.040 --> 00:09:55.960
It can take a while to build. Nobody

00:09:53.760 --> 00:09:57.760
ever teaches us this in school. I have

00:09:55.960 --> 00:09:59.680
met older adults who don't even know

00:09:57.760 --> 00:10:02.000
about building credit, for example. So,

00:09:59.680 --> 00:10:04.400
real quick, FICO score is 35% payment

00:10:02.000 --> 00:10:07.640
history, 30% how much you owe, 15% how

00:10:04.400 --> 00:10:10.000
long you've got credit, 10% and 10% your

00:10:07.640 --> 00:10:12.160
mix. So, the biggest piece is just not

00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:13.920
missing payments. Setting up auto pay

00:10:12.160 --> 00:10:15.440
for at least the minimum on every card

00:10:13.920 --> 00:10:17.360
is one of the highest return 10 minutes

00:10:15.440 --> 00:10:18.840
of your adult life. But I also recommend

00:10:17.360 --> 00:10:21.080
paying off the monthly balance as a

00:10:18.840 --> 00:10:23.200
habit if you can, so you don't rack up

00:10:21.080 --> 00:10:25.840
hidden interest fees. Also, while you're

00:10:23.200 --> 00:10:28.520
here, learn how compound interest works.

00:10:25.840 --> 00:10:30.800
The idea that money can earn interest on

00:10:28.520 --> 00:10:32.560
its interest. One afternoon of learning

00:10:30.800 --> 00:10:35.320
this can shape the rate that you get on

00:10:32.560 --> 00:10:37.440
a car, an apartment, a home, for the

00:10:35.320 --> 00:10:39.120
rest of your decades. Number eight,

00:10:37.440 --> 00:10:41.400
negotiating your bills. In fact,

00:10:39.120 --> 00:10:42.960
negotiation is one of the best skills

00:10:41.400 --> 00:10:44.880
you can learn in life. This will make

00:10:42.960 --> 00:10:46.600
you money or give you more money back.

00:10:44.880 --> 00:10:48.640
So, if you want to practice, start small

00:10:46.600 --> 00:10:50.560
with bills. This is such a great hack,

00:10:48.640 --> 00:10:53.000
especially if you have options on your

00:10:50.560 --> 00:10:55.160
providers. Call your phone or internet

00:10:53.000 --> 00:10:56.640
provider and ask them what promotions

00:10:55.160 --> 00:10:57.760
you have for existing customers. I've

00:10:56.640 --> 00:10:59.560
been looking at switching to a different

00:10:57.760 --> 00:11:00.880
service provider. Or better yet, if

00:10:59.560 --> 00:11:02.800
you've already found a service that's

00:11:00.880 --> 00:11:04.600
cheaper. Worst case, they say no, we

00:11:02.800 --> 00:11:05.960
don't, and you lost five minutes, fine.

00:11:04.600 --> 00:11:07.680
Best case, you just saved yourself a

00:11:05.960 --> 00:11:09.160
bunch of money for the next few years.

00:11:07.680 --> 00:11:11.120
Another good low-risk way to learn

00:11:09.160 --> 00:11:13.080
negotiation is by haggling at the

00:11:11.120 --> 00:11:14.600
market, maybe flea market or vintage

00:11:13.080 --> 00:11:16.960
fair. There's a difference in how

00:11:14.600 --> 00:11:18.640
successful you can be, depending on the

00:11:16.960 --> 00:11:20.160
day and the time that you're showing up,

00:11:18.640 --> 00:11:21.880
how many items you're buying, and even

00:11:20.160 --> 00:11:23.680
by looking at the face of the seller and

00:11:21.880 --> 00:11:25.720
reading them. I will get into how we can

00:11:23.680 --> 00:11:27.760
do that in detail later. Same thing with

00:11:25.720 --> 00:11:29.360
your salary. If you work full-time, for

00:11:27.760 --> 00:11:30.960
freelancers and business owners, you're

00:11:29.360 --> 00:11:33.160
setting your own rates. But when it

00:11:30.960 --> 00:11:35.680
comes to wages, always, always

00:11:33.160 --> 00:11:37.800
negotiate. And never negotiate against

00:11:35.680 --> 00:11:40.120
yourself. For example, one sentence you

00:11:37.800 --> 00:11:41.480
can say is, "Is there flexibility on

00:11:40.120 --> 00:11:43.520
this number?" And I'm speaking as

00:11:41.480 --> 00:11:44.480
someone who used to hire people. If they

00:11:43.520 --> 00:11:46.040
say no, they're not going to

00:11:44.480 --> 00:11:48.640
automatically rule you out just cuz you

00:11:46.040 --> 00:11:51.000
asked. Your employers almost always

00:11:48.640 --> 00:11:52.648
expect you to negotiate your salary. And

00:11:51.000 --> 00:11:54.400
by not negotiating, you're automatically

00:11:52.648 --> 00:11:56.320
[clears throat] saving them money. Now,

00:11:54.400 --> 00:11:58.880
tier three is going to be hobbies that

00:11:56.320 --> 00:12:00.640
give back. Number nine is having one

00:11:58.880 --> 00:12:02.160
analog hobby with your hands. Whether

00:12:00.640 --> 00:12:03.720
that's pottery, knitting, sketching,

00:12:02.160 --> 00:12:04.960
baking bread. Better yet, if it's

00:12:03.720 --> 00:12:07.160
something that doesn't come with any

00:12:04.960 --> 00:12:08.720
strings attached. Because why do we turn

00:12:07.160 --> 00:12:10.840
every hobby into a performance or

00:12:08.720 --> 00:12:13.960
money-making scheme? This is the one

00:12:10.840 --> 00:12:15.760
thing you do just to feel like a normal

00:12:13.960 --> 00:12:17.840
person. So, moving your hands while your

00:12:15.760 --> 00:12:19.680
mind wanders, that is actually one of

00:12:17.840 --> 00:12:22.000
the most gentle ways out of a thought

00:12:19.680 --> 00:12:24.320
loop or an anxiety spiral that you might

00:12:22.000 --> 00:12:25.920
have been stuck in for weeks. For me,

00:12:24.320 --> 00:12:27.760
that's been swimming and reading books.

00:12:25.920 --> 00:12:29.520
I also paint every now and then. It is

00:12:27.760 --> 00:12:31.120
super therapeutic for me because I don't

00:12:29.520 --> 00:12:33.040
try to be good at it. I have no

00:12:31.120 --> 00:12:35.400
expectations to be good. In fact, we all

00:12:33.040 --> 00:12:37.920
need to get better at being bad at

00:12:35.400 --> 00:12:40.920
things. That's the secret to getting rid

00:12:37.920 --> 00:12:43.240
of perfectionism. So, one rule to keep

00:12:40.920 --> 00:12:45.240
to yourself, don't monetize it. At least

00:12:43.240 --> 00:12:47.600
not just yet, but maybe not ever. These

00:12:45.240 --> 00:12:50.240
hobbies that you don't monetize pays you

00:12:47.600 --> 00:12:52.080
back in aura. Think about it. Number 10,

00:12:50.240 --> 00:12:53.480
call your elders just to say hi. And

00:12:52.080 --> 00:12:55.720
this is something I think about a lot as

00:12:53.480 --> 00:12:57.400
I get older. How many more chances do we

00:12:55.720 --> 00:12:59.360
get to talk to our elder family members

00:12:57.400 --> 00:13:01.080
in this lifetime? For example, calling

00:12:59.360 --> 00:13:02.800
your family members just to say hi, tell

00:13:01.080 --> 00:13:05.280
them you love them, that can make their

00:13:02.800 --> 00:13:07.960
entire day. In experiments with nearly

00:13:05.280 --> 00:13:10.000
6,000 people, the people who reach out

00:13:07.960 --> 00:13:11.680
consistently underestimated how much the

00:13:10.000 --> 00:13:13.839
other person appreciated it. And the

00:13:11.680 --> 00:13:16.680
more unexpected the call, the more it

00:13:13.839 --> 00:13:18.640
meant to them. Better yet, ask them what

00:13:16.680 --> 00:13:20.520
they were like at your age. Ask them

00:13:18.640 --> 00:13:22.360
about the family stories, maybe even do

00:13:20.520 --> 00:13:24.880
an interview because their stories are

00:13:22.360 --> 00:13:27.520
yours, too. Whatever they struggled with

00:13:24.880 --> 00:13:30.240
and overcame, that's in your DNA.

00:13:27.520 --> 00:13:32.360
Literally, it is. Knowing those stories

00:13:30.240 --> 00:13:34.800
will help you understand yourself better

00:13:32.360 --> 00:13:37.040
and why you are the way you are. There's

00:13:34.800 --> 00:13:38.560
a version of you, maybe years or even

00:13:37.040 --> 00:13:41.080
decades from now, that would give

00:13:38.560 --> 00:13:43.200
anything for one more of these calls

00:13:41.080 --> 00:13:44.960
someday. So, make it while you can.

00:13:43.200 --> 00:13:47.320
Don't wait till it's too late. Tier four

00:13:44.960 --> 00:13:49.160
is the go-to tier, it's the multipliers.

00:13:47.320 --> 00:13:51.520
The first hand gives you back time,

00:13:49.160 --> 00:13:53.280
health, and peace. These last five are a

00:13:51.520 --> 00:13:55.040
different category all together. They

00:13:53.280 --> 00:13:57.120
are the ones that break the game, they

00:13:55.040 --> 00:13:59.440
multiply everything, and it's basically

00:13:57.120 --> 00:14:01.680
understanding the way people work.

00:13:59.440 --> 00:14:04.200
Number 11, learn sales and marketing.

00:14:01.680 --> 00:14:05.680
Everything in life is a pitch. Your job

00:14:04.200 --> 00:14:07.480
interview is a pitch, your boundaries

00:14:05.680 --> 00:14:09.280
are a pitch, asking for a raise, getting

00:14:07.480 --> 00:14:11.160
your family member to try therapy,

00:14:09.280 --> 00:14:13.880
starting a business, going on a dating

00:14:11.160 --> 00:14:15.160
app, it is all a pitch. I learned this

00:14:13.880 --> 00:14:17.200
working in nightlife in New York, where

00:14:15.160 --> 00:14:18.840
the job is to get people to say yes to a

00:14:17.200 --> 00:14:21.000
fun night that hasn't happened yet.

00:14:18.840 --> 00:14:22.960
Selling is all about translating what

00:14:21.000 --> 00:14:25.200
you know is valuable into what someone

00:14:22.960 --> 00:14:26.640
else actually cares about. If you can't

00:14:25.200 --> 00:14:29.200
sell an idea, then you're not

00:14:26.640 --> 00:14:31.000
convincing. The most convincing person

00:14:29.200 --> 00:14:32.720
gets what they want. In fact, you can

00:14:31.000 --> 00:14:35.760
say they can get whatever they want. So,

00:14:32.720 --> 00:14:37.839
every day, practice noticing one ad that

00:14:35.760 --> 00:14:40.600
made you want to buy something, and ask

00:14:37.839 --> 00:14:42.680
yourself why. Then, practice explaining

00:14:40.600 --> 00:14:44.800
an idea you came up with in one single

00:14:42.680 --> 00:14:47.535
sentence. Number 12, communication.

00:14:44.800 --> 00:14:49.280
Saying what you need out loud. Most

00:14:47.535 --> 00:14:51.760
[snorts] resentment is a need that you

00:14:49.280 --> 00:14:54.320
never said to anyone. If we're waiting

00:14:51.760 --> 00:14:56.600
around for people to guess and read our

00:14:54.320 --> 00:14:58.440
minds and hint, and then we're hurt when

00:14:56.600 --> 00:15:00.640
they don't get it right. Here's a

00:14:58.440 --> 00:15:04.120
sentence that you can steal. I feel

00:15:00.640 --> 00:15:06.360
blank when blank, and what I need is

00:15:04.120 --> 00:15:08.360
blank. It may feel a little bit clunky

00:15:06.360 --> 00:15:09.760
at first, then it becomes the reason

00:15:08.360 --> 00:15:12.760
your relationship start running on

00:15:09.760 --> 00:15:15.160
silent score keeping. Number 13, reading

00:15:12.760 --> 00:15:17.600
people and situations. This is the skill

00:15:15.160 --> 00:15:20.520
that makes people want you in every

00:15:17.600 --> 00:15:22.240
room, because the library is open, you

00:15:20.520 --> 00:15:24.760
are a librarian, and you know how to

00:15:22.240 --> 00:15:27.640
read the room and read people. This will

00:15:24.760 --> 00:15:29.000
get you so far ahead in life. Let's say

00:15:27.640 --> 00:15:30.880
you're in a meeting, you notice who

00:15:29.000 --> 00:15:32.440
hasn't spoken in the last 20 minutes and

00:15:30.880 --> 00:15:34.680
you know why. You also know what your

00:15:32.440 --> 00:15:36.480
boss is secretly stressed about or you

00:15:34.680 --> 00:15:38.840
see someone who's constantly being left

00:15:36.480 --> 00:15:40.360
out. The person who can notice all of

00:15:38.840 --> 00:15:42.960
these little things and know how to

00:15:40.360 --> 00:15:45.120
approach these people gets remembered.

00:15:42.960 --> 00:15:47.160
They also get hired, invited back to the

00:15:45.120 --> 00:15:48.480
functions, they get trusted. You know, I

00:15:47.160 --> 00:15:50.080
actually thought about this last night

00:15:48.480 --> 00:15:52.000
and I'm about to go into a dark place

00:15:50.080 --> 00:15:54.680
but whatever. If I ever have kids and I

00:15:52.000 --> 00:15:57.280
live in America, I need to train my kids

00:15:54.680 --> 00:15:59.320
as young as possible to be especially

00:15:57.280 --> 00:16:01.800
kind to their schoolmates who get

00:15:59.320 --> 00:16:03.600
othered or bullied because I was one of

00:16:01.800 --> 00:16:06.000
them, I knew what it felt like and if

00:16:03.600 --> 00:16:08.680
something happens, knock on wood, and

00:16:06.000 --> 00:16:11.680
there's some kind of at school, they may

00:16:08.680 --> 00:16:14.360
even be spared. Sometimes the status quo

00:16:11.680 --> 00:16:16.320
is actually not the safest place to be.

00:16:14.360 --> 00:16:18.280
So, do this practice. Every time you

00:16:16.320 --> 00:16:20.360
walk into a room, ask yourself, what is

00:16:18.280 --> 00:16:22.640
the goal that is in everyone's head and

00:16:20.360 --> 00:16:24.760
then turn it inward as well. What do I

00:16:22.640 --> 00:16:26.560
need right now? What's my goal? How do I

00:16:24.760 --> 00:16:28.440
get to my goal and also help other

00:16:26.560 --> 00:16:29.839
people get to theirs? Doesn't matter if

00:16:28.440 --> 00:16:32.680
it's work or school, this is such a

00:16:29.839 --> 00:16:34.880
passive way to provide immense value.

00:16:32.680 --> 00:16:36.520
Number 14, critical thinking and nuance,

00:16:34.880 --> 00:16:38.080
learning how the world works because two

00:16:36.520 --> 00:16:39.520
things can be true at the same time. We

00:16:38.080 --> 00:16:41.920
know this but a lot of people don't

00:16:39.520 --> 00:16:43.480
actually know in practice. The people

00:16:41.920 --> 00:16:45.120
who I've observed who really get ahead

00:16:43.480 --> 00:16:47.480
in life are the ones who also understand

00:16:45.120 --> 00:16:49.360
nuances and critical thinking. They

00:16:47.480 --> 00:16:51.360
don't teach enough of this in school and

00:16:49.360 --> 00:16:53.760
because of social media and online

00:16:51.360 --> 00:16:56.480
discourse and most of us existing in

00:16:53.760 --> 00:16:58.720
bubbles, we are ending up with a lot of

00:16:56.480 --> 00:17:01.400
one-track mind, black and white thinking

00:16:58.720 --> 00:17:03.160
which causes a lot of division and

00:17:01.400 --> 00:17:05.920
that's really making us miss out on

00:17:03.160 --> 00:17:08.160
developing nuance which is dangerous. A

00:17:05.920 --> 00:17:09.680
lot of it is reading between the lines.

00:17:08.160 --> 00:17:11.920
How do we train that? This is where

00:17:09.680 --> 00:17:13.439
reading comes in. 10 minutes a day of

00:17:11.920 --> 00:17:15.800
something that explains how something

00:17:13.439 --> 00:17:18.240
works, money, history, psychology, why

00:17:15.800 --> 00:17:21.040
companies do what they do, why people

00:17:18.240 --> 00:17:23.199
succeed, and every so often read the

00:17:21.040 --> 00:17:25.880
most intelligent version of an opinion

00:17:23.199 --> 00:17:28.240
that you disagree with. You need to get

00:17:25.880 --> 00:17:30.720
comfortable with unpopular opinions and

00:17:28.240 --> 00:17:33.560
understand the perspectives of people

00:17:30.720 --> 00:17:35.680
that you so-called hate. Because if you

00:17:33.560 --> 00:17:37.560
don't, you're also missing out on the

00:17:35.680 --> 00:17:40.440
perspectives of a huge chunk of the

00:17:37.560 --> 00:17:42.600
population. We do not exist in a silo.

00:17:40.440 --> 00:17:44.720
All of us make up our society. So if you

00:17:42.600 --> 00:17:46.640
understand the people who you don't

00:17:44.720 --> 00:17:49.280
agree with, you will know how to

00:17:46.640 --> 00:17:51.520
approach all kinds of situations. People

00:17:49.280 --> 00:17:54.680
who are easily rage-baited, so to speak,

00:17:51.520 --> 00:17:57.080
and reactive are also easily controlled

00:17:54.680 --> 00:17:59.160
and manipulated. So this is a shortcut

00:17:57.080 --> 00:18:00.920
that I use when you don't understand why

00:17:59.160 --> 00:18:03.760
something you don't like is happening,

00:18:00.920 --> 00:18:05.640
follow the incentive. Who is benefiting

00:18:03.760 --> 00:18:07.760
from this? It will explain pretty much

00:18:05.640 --> 00:18:09.480
everything. Number 15, study people as

00:18:07.760 --> 00:18:10.680
walking contradictions. This might even

00:18:09.480 --> 00:18:13.280
be the most important part of the whole

00:18:10.680 --> 00:18:15.240
video. People are inherently walking

00:18:13.280 --> 00:18:16.600
contradictions. It is in our humanity.

00:18:15.240 --> 00:18:18.880
It doesn't make anyone inherently good

00:18:16.600 --> 00:18:20.320
or bad, especially because everyone

00:18:18.880 --> 00:18:22.560
thinks they're good. So we need to

00:18:20.320 --> 00:18:23.920
understand why, for example, a friend

00:18:22.560 --> 00:18:26.400
who can't shut up about being kind to

00:18:23.920 --> 00:18:28.720
people is being mean to service industry

00:18:26.400 --> 00:18:31.160
people, or why someone who says that

00:18:28.720 --> 00:18:33.360
they hate drama is somehow in all of the

00:18:31.160 --> 00:18:35.160
dramas. We need to learn how to stop

00:18:33.360 --> 00:18:37.200
being shocked when that happens and

00:18:35.160 --> 00:18:39.400
learn to work with it. Otherwise, we

00:18:37.200 --> 00:18:41.320
will be constantly extremely disgruntled

00:18:39.400 --> 00:18:42.680
and disappointed and upset at people

00:18:41.320 --> 00:18:45.160
because you're not matching up to how

00:18:42.680 --> 00:18:47.120
we're seeing them. In stoicism, nobody

00:18:45.160 --> 00:18:49.080
is better or worse than anyone. We're

00:18:47.120 --> 00:18:51.040
not putting anyone on the pedestal, not

00:18:49.080 --> 00:18:53.160
even me. Please, I don't want that. I'm

00:18:51.040 --> 00:18:55.320
a person, too. We're all flawed human

00:18:53.160 --> 00:18:57.680
beings. So instead of listening, watch

00:18:55.320 --> 00:18:59.840
what people do, okay? The reason why

00:18:57.680 --> 00:19:01.320
people become bullies is not only

00:18:59.840 --> 00:19:02.760
because they want to feel superior to

00:19:01.320 --> 00:19:05.080
others in order to regain a sense of

00:19:02.760 --> 00:19:07.440
control over their lives, but also they

00:19:05.080 --> 00:19:09.440
are repressing a shadow side of them

00:19:07.440 --> 00:19:12.280
they don't want to acknowledge. When the

00:19:09.440 --> 00:19:15.120
shadow of ours is suppressed, it comes

00:19:12.280 --> 00:19:16.520
up as projection. It always comes up. If

00:19:15.120 --> 00:19:18.640
you're someone who's constantly being

00:19:16.520 --> 00:19:21.280
projected on, for example, that means

00:19:18.640 --> 00:19:23.760
you're triggering deep insecurities in

00:19:21.280 --> 00:19:26.600
other people, and these people will

00:19:23.760 --> 00:19:28.520
never admit it. So, understand that for

00:19:26.600 --> 00:19:30.160
what it is. And when people tell you

00:19:28.520 --> 00:19:31.880
their opinions and their point of view,

00:19:30.160 --> 00:19:34.160
they're also telling you how they're

00:19:31.880 --> 00:19:36.480
eventually treat you when it's your

00:19:34.160 --> 00:19:38.280
turn. This includes the way people talk

00:19:36.480 --> 00:19:40.160
about their exes, how they talk about

00:19:38.280 --> 00:19:41.760
people who can't help them in any way,

00:19:40.160 --> 00:19:43.280
or whether everyone in their life is the

00:19:41.760 --> 00:19:44.880
